From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: =?UTF-8?q?Enrico=20B=C3=BChler?= <enrico.buehler@unom.io>
Date: Fri, 2 Oct 2026 18:25:17 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 31/33] pipewire: offer the 10-bit capture formats as SDR too

The packed 10-bit formats and P010 have carried a MANDATORY
BT.2020 + PQ description since they were added, so a consumer
that wants 10-bit SDR cannot have it: the SDR composite is 8-bit
only, and a Main10 SDR stream widens an 8-bit capture.

Offer each 10-bit format a second time, after the HDR pod, with
BT.709 primaries and the sRGB-family transfer the SDR composite
writes (P010: BT.709 matrix, limited or full range). The HDR pods
keep their MANDATORY colorimetry and stay first, so a consumer that
names nothing lands where it always did. paint_pipewire keys the
PQ LUT set on the negotiated transfer function instead of the DRM
format; the P010 pass applies a 10-bit BT.709 matrix on the sRGB
codes an SDR composite stores. Every YCbCr capture already
composites through the 10-bit RGB intermediate, so the SDR stream
carries the composite's own precision.

Stamp pfhdr26.
